            "body": "> > The feature treats concealed cells as taking no space.\r\n> \r\n> Only when concealing is active for a line. If a line is unconcealed due to 'concealcursor' then concealed cells will take space.\r\n\r\nCorrect. That's what I'm referring to. I guess I could have been clearer in my argument. As the code is now, when the cursor is NOT on the line, the decision to ignore conceal at the tab feels wrong. It's something my original PR addressed but this one opts to leave out. Not sure if that was an oversight or intentional.",
