            "body": "> ```\r\n> - [Docs](https://neovim.io/doc)<Tab>Reference\r\n> - Intro<Tab>Overview\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> With `tabstop=8`, `conceallevel=2` and the link markup concealed by extmarks, master and this PR both render:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> - Docs                          Reference\r\n> - Intro Overview\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> ...\r\n> \r\n> If the Tab used the displayed column, both lines would line up:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> - Docs  Reference\r\n> - Intro Overview\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThanks for that callout. How common is that though? And in any case it is something that should be a followup, so the initial PR stays focused.\r\n\r\nOTOH not sure that feature is actually desired, it would cause the text to bounce around, and if such concealment were in e.g. a table heading, the table columns would not be aligned... Current behavior:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4dbc3c2-8181-453f-86fc-ededc5390811\r\n\r\n\r\n",
