        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> Thanks for that callout. How common is that though? And in any case it is something that should be a followup, so the initial PR stays focused.\r\n> \r\n> OTOH not sure that feature is actually desired, it would cause the text to bounce around, and if such concealment were in e.g. a table heading, the table columns would not be aligned... Current behavior:\r\n\r\nI agree with your question on desirability. The documentation/spec isn't really clear either and there's sound arguments both ways. Maybe a follow-up is best.",
